            <ArticleTitle>The importance of screening for healthy weight and recommending healthy lifestyles in pediatric patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>34-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Regular pediatric care should focus on early obesity prevention and healthy lifestyles and should include obesity screening with sensitive and culturally appropriate communication, beginning at age 2 years. North Carolina is a leader with its Eat Smart, Move More campaign and tools that can help pediatric care providers achieve greater self-efficacy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
